course: dictionary
lesson: 12918
title: Hard feelings and families apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Estrangement is when people who used to be close stop speaking or seeing each other. It is most often used for family members. «After the argument, Mia and her father had years of estrangement.» The clues are argument and years: they were close once, something went wrong, and they stayed apart for a long time.
explain: The word estranged is the adjective. «Her estranged brother never came to visit.» Estranged tells you the brother used to be part of her life, but now they are not in touch. Estrangement is the noun, the state of being apart.
explain: Estrangement can also mean a feeling of being cut off from something. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. If you are unsure, ask a grown-up or check a dictionary.
fact: Estrangement means being cut off from people you used to be close to.
fact: Estrangement is a noun. Estranged is the adjective, and it describes a person.
fact: «Years of estrangement» means a very long time apart, without speaking.
fact: «Estranged» means no longer close, often in a family.
fact: Clue words like argument, years and never often show that estrangement is a sad, serious thing.
exercise: «After the argument, Mia and her father had years of estrangement.» What does estrangement mean? | Learning to swim | Being very rich | A big family party | *Being cut off from someone you used to be close to
exercise: «Her estranged brother never came to visit.» What does estranged suggest? | *Used to be close, but no longer in touch | Newly married | Sleeping in the same room | Always laughing together
exercise: «Grandma and I had not spoken for years.» Find and copy one word that tells you how long. | *years | grandma | spoken | had
test:
Which word describes a person who is no longer close to their family? | estranged | *estranged, not estrangement | distant road | lonely
A child says, «My dad and I have been in estrangement for years.» What does this mean? | *We have not been close or in touch for a long time | We go fishing together every weekend | We live in the same house | We are celebrating an anniversary
exam: Which sentence uses the word estrangement correctly? | The estrangement cooked a big dinner for everyone. | We went to estrangement at the beach on Saturday. | She won first prize in the estrangement race. | *The estrangement between the two brothers lasted ten years.
